WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.172 --> 00:00:23.197
is so embarrassing," Iris thought as she missed another ball that Jae lobbed her way.

2
00:00:24.058 --> 00:00:28.261
She wished she had paired up with Javier—or anyone else.

3
00:00:28.281 --> 00:00:34.254
"I probably just need to warm up a little," she called to Jae with a nervous laugh.

4
00:00:35.315 --> 00:00:37.717
She exhaled and tried to relax.

5
00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.679
She took another swing.

6
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.621
Another miss.

7
00:00:42.641 --> 00:00:45.984
"Or maybe this racket has a hole in it!"

8
00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:47.225
she joked.

9
00:00:47.245 --> 00:00:48.847
"Could be."

10
00:00:49.807 --> 00:00:52.129
Jae shrugged and hit another ball to her.

11
00:00:53.731 --> 00:00:56.253
Iris swung—and missed again.

12
00:00:58.315 --> 00:00:59.656
Jae scratched his head.

13
00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.041
"Didn't you say your soccer team made it to the state playoffs?"

14
00:01:06.081 --> 00:01:09.282
"The key word there is soccer," Iris said.

15
00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:13.543
"And trust me, tennis is nothing like soccer."

16
00:01:14.664 --> 00:01:17.204
She looked down and inspected her racket.

17
00:01:17.224 --> 00:01:20.045
"Maybe I need a different one of these."

18
00:01:20.065 --> 00:01:24.666
"Having a problem over here?"

19
00:01:25.287 --> 00:01:28.487
Trent appeared from behind Iris, making her jump.

20
00:01:28.507 --> 00:01:30.228
"A problem?

21
00:01:31.652 --> 00:01:34.474
Uh Iris didn't know what to say.

22
00:01:35.215 --> 00:01:37.937
Instinctively, she glanced over at Javier.

23
00:01:41.179 --> 00:01:47.163
He was swinging his racket like crazy but not coming any closer to hitting the ball than she

24
00:01:47.223 --> 00:01:49.885
was. Trent followed her gaze.

25
00:01:50.526 --> 00:01:54.348
"You and Javier have never played tennis before, have you?"

26
00:01:54.368 --> 00:01:56.990
"Nope," Iris said.

27
00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.412
"Not even table tennis!"

28
00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.462
She grinned at Jae, and he chuckled.

29
00:02:02.482 --> 00:02:05.204
"It's okay."

30
00:02:05.864 --> 00:02:09.366
But Trent was frowning like it really wasn't okay.

31
00:02:09.386 --> 00:02:13.769
"Jae, why don't you partner up with Zoe instead?"

32
00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.492
He pointed at the blond girl hitting balls at Javier.

33
00:02:19.093 --> 00:02:21.815
Zoe heard Trent and turned to face them.

34
00:02:23.156 --> 00:02:25.598
Her face was already lit up into a smile.

35
00:02:25.618 --> 00:02:27.679
"Great idea!"

36
00:02:28.279 --> 00:02:28.820
she called.

37
00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.081
Jae flashed Zoe a grin.

38
00:02:31.101 --> 00:02:33.022
"Sure," he said.

39
00:02:33.042 --> 00:02:34.322
"Sounds good."

40
00:02:35.303 --> 00:02:37.584
Iris felt a flush creep up her face.

41
00:02:38.244 --> 00:02:39.905
Zoe was very pretty.

42
00:02:40.865 --> 00:02:47.268
Jae seemed very happy to be Zoe's partner, and Zoe looked just as happy to be partners with

43
00:02:47.349 --> 00:02:52.111
him. "You two can start practicing," Trent said to them.

44
00:02:52.711 --> 00:02:54.432
Then he waved Javier over.

45
00:02:57.208 --> 00:03:02.691
"I know Julie said we'd figure out the groups after tryouts, but there's no sense in keeping the

46
00:03:02.731 --> 00:03:03.552
two of you here.

47
00:03:04.392 --> 00:03:07.234
You really need to learn the basics of tennis first.

48
00:03:08.094 --> 00:03:10.836
Besides, the other group has fewer kids."

49
00:03:12.397 --> 00:03:17.540
He pointed to another court, where Ally stood observing the younger campers.

50
00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.922
"Just head on over there, and tell Ally I sent you."

51
00:03:22.623 --> 00:03:24.804
He turned back to the rest of the older group.

52
00:03:27.384 --> 00:03:28.305
Iris blinked.

53
00:03:29.345 --> 00:03:32.386
Trent had just sent them down to the baby class!

54
00:03:33.587 --> 00:03:38.089
She inspected her racket once more before following Javier off the court.

55
00:03:38.989 --> 00:03:41.670
Her brother didn't seem to be bothered in the slightest.

56
00:03:42.591 --> 00:03:46.852
Of course, he wasn't used to excelling at sports like Iris was.

57
00:03:47.753 --> 00:03:50.114
And this was about more than tennis.

58
00:03:50.854 --> 00:03:51.995
Jae was cute.

59
00:03:53.055 --> 00:03:54.916
She wanted to be in his group.

60
00:03:55.688 --> 00:04:00.091
So Iris had to learn how to play tennis—and learn fast.

61
00:04:02.052 --> 00:04:04.533
Ally saw Iris and Javier approaching.

62
00:04:04.553 --> 00:04:07.835
"What's up?"

63
00:04:07.855 --> 00:04:12.238
"Trent sent us to join your group," Iris mumbled.

64
00:04:12.258 --> 00:04:16.520
"We've never played tennis before," Javier said.

65
00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:19.622
"Oh, that's fine," Ally said.

66
00:04:19.642 --> 00:04:25.825
"His group had too many kids anyway, and we can definitely teach you some stuff over here."

67
00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.887
She waved at some kids who were playing on the court.

68
00:04:30.847 --> 00:04:32.168
Grace! Ben!

69
00:04:32.908 --> 00:04:34.509
Can you come over here for a minute?"

70
00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:44.213
Grace and Ben each stood about a head shorter than Iris, and their identical blond hair and blue

71
00:04:44.373 --> 00:04:48.635
eyes made them seem like polar opposites of Iris and Javier.

72
00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:55.347
"Twins?" All four kids blurted out the word at the same time.

73
00:04:56.348 --> 00:04:57.149
Ally laughed.

74
00:04:57.169 --> 00:05:01.893
"Yes! The four of you will be perfect teammates."

75
00:05:03.194 --> 00:05:09.859
Iris smiled as politely as she could, but the idea that these kids were her new teammates was

76
00:05:09.959 --> 00:05:10.980
kind of insulting.

77
00:05:12.061 --> 00:05:14.003
They looked about nine years old.

78
00:05:14.823 --> 00:05:16.384
Grace smiled at Iris.

79
00:05:16.405 --> 00:05:18.266
"Do you want to come with me?"

80
00:05:19.507 --> 00:05:20.328
Iris shrugged.

81
00:05:21.208 --> 00:05:22.889
"I guess," she mumbled.

82
00:05:22.909 --> 00:05:26.870
"So I must be with you," Javier said to Ben.

83
00:05:27.911 --> 00:05:29.271
Iris stared at her brother.

84
00:05:30.032 --> 00:05:32.673
He was giving the younger boy a friendly smile.

85
00:05:32.693 --> 00:05:38.215
"Javier seriously doesn't care that we're stuck playing with these little kids!"

86
00:05:38.955 --> 00:05:39.556
Iris thought.

87
00:05:39.576 --> 00:05:41.916
"Why isn't he embarrassed?"

88
00:05:41.936 --> 00:05:47.359
"Grace and Ben went to our junior camp last year," Ally said.

89
00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:50.520
"They won the final match for their age group."

90
00:05:52.032 --> 00:05:53.673
"Wow," Javier said.

91
00:05:53.693 --> 00:05:56.675
"Cool." Iris swallowed.

92
00:05:56.695 --> 00:05:59.877
"Great," she thought.

93
00:06:00.737 --> 00:06:06.600
Not only were they stuck with these babies, but these babies actually knew how to play tennis!

94
00:06:07.781 --> 00:06:10.802
Grace led Iris to an empty space on the court.

95
00:06:10.822 --> 00:06:16.806
"You guys must be pretty bad if they sent you down to our group!"

96
00:06:17.386 --> 00:06:17.926
she joked.

97
00:06:17.946 --> 00:06:21.933
"We've never played before, that's all," Iris said.

98
00:06:21.953 --> 00:06:24.655
"Once I learn what to do, I'll be fine."

99
00:06:24.675 --> 00:06:26.737
"Well, don't worry."

100
00:06:27.157 --> 00:06:28.038
Grace smiled.

101
00:06:28.058 --> 00:06:30.280
"Ally's a great coach."

102
00:06:31.741 --> 00:06:33.082
Ally jogged over to them.

103
00:06:33.102 --> 00:06:37.446
"First things first," she said.

104
00:06:37.466 --> 00:06:40.028
"Let me see your swing, Iris."

105
00:06:41.069 --> 00:06:45.993
Iris gripped the racket in both hands and gave it a powerful swing.

106
00:06:46.013 --> 00:06:49.756
"Uh-uh." Grace shook her head.

107
00:06:50.444 --> 00:06:52.084
"You're doing it all wrong."

108
00:06:53.145 --> 00:06:54.065
Iris flushed.

109
00:06:54.085 --> 00:06:57.206
"Here, watch me," Ally said.

110
00:06:57.846 --> 00:07:00.287
She planted her own feet hip-width apart.

111
00:07:02.087 --> 00:07:07.088
With one hip facing the net, she held her racket gently with both hands.

112
00:07:08.549 --> 00:07:14.931
When she swung, she shifted her weight gracefully toward the net, almost as though she was dancing with

113
00:07:14.971 --> 00:07:15.531
her racket.

114
00:07:15.551 --> 00:07:23.346
"So that's how you swing," Ally went on, "but you also have to pay attention to the ball."

115
00:07:25.088 --> 00:07:29.271
She tossed a tennis ball up in the air and caught it with the same hand.

116
00:07:29.291 --> 00:07:36.197
"Get ready, toss the ball, shift your weight, and swing!"

117
00:07:38.118 --> 00:07:41.962
Her racket struck the ball and lobbed it a few feet in front of her.

118
00:07:41.982 --> 00:07:47.947
"Maybe Iris should just focus on her swing for now," Grace suggested.

119
00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:50.589
"Sure," Ally said.

120
00:07:50.609 --> 00:07:52.110
"Good idea, Grace.

121
00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:54.011
I need to check on Javier."

122
00:07:54.972 --> 00:08:01.378
For the rest of the morning, Grace gave Iris tips as Iris practiced her swing and hit the

123
00:08:01.418 --> 00:08:03.159
ball against a practice wall.

124
00:08:07.663 --> 00:08:13.808
She made some slow progress, but there was a lot to remember, and they hadn't even started to

125
00:08:13.868 --> 00:08:15.289
play against each other yet!

126
00:08:15.309 --> 00:08:18.652
"Lunchtime!" Ally called.

127
00:08:20.272 --> 00:08:22.413
"Phew!" Iris thought.

128
00:08:22.433 --> 00:08:25.454
"Practice is finally over."

129
00:08:26.575 --> 00:08:31.917
She let out a sigh and followed Grace to the shady picnic tables where they'd all left their

130
00:08:31.977 --> 00:08:33.758
backpacks and lunches that morning.

131
00:08:37.199 --> 00:08:39.080
Jae was standing near her stuff.

132
00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:41.421
Iris' heartbeat sped up.

133
00:08:42.381 --> 00:08:46.403
They were in different groups now, but maybe they could still be friends.

134
00:08:47.423 --> 00:08:51.204
Before she could call out to him, he smiled at Zoe.

135
00:08:52.045 --> 00:08:53.485
"Ready?" he asked her.

136
00:08:53.505 --> 00:08:56.486
"Ready!" Zoe replied.

137
00:08:57.346 --> 00:09:02.088
Jae glanced quickly in Iris' direction, as if he knew she was there.

138
00:09:03.368 --> 00:09:07.729
But instead of saying anything to her, he simply looked away.
